---
/**
 * About (/ngo/about) — NGO "Who We Are". Built against Figma node 7429:5025.
 *
 * ⚠ REDESIGNED 2026-08-07. The page was first built (Phase 3, docs/ngo-build-plan.md) against the
 * 2026-07-20 ingest, which is what design/figma/…/7429-5025/node.json still holds. The frame has
 * since been reworked and that snapshot is STALE — it is 5547px tall where the live frame is
 * 4066px. This build follows the LIVE node, read through the Figma MCP; every value below was
 * confirmed against it, not against the committed node.json. Re-run `npm run figma:fetch` (needs
 * FIGMA_API_KEY) to resync the snapshot. What changed, and is now reflected here:
 *   - A full-bleed photo hero + "Who We Are" h1 replaced the white "HOME / ABOUT" breadcrumb
 *     header. The breadcrumb is gone from the design entirely.
 *   - The boat photo that opened the intro is gone; the section starts on the "Our Story" h2.
 *   - Core Values became five title-case headings with descriptive paragraphs in a 2-col grid,
 *     replacing five bare all-caps labels. The source's own typos were fixed upstream —
 *     "INTERGRITY"→"Integrity", "EMPOERMENT"→"Empowerment" — and "INCLUSIVENESS" became
 *     "Inclusivity", a different word, not a re-spelling. "Mision" was NOT fixed and is still
 *     misspelled in the live design, so it stays verbatim here (exact-replica-first).
 *   - The entire Core Team section (eyebrow, "Every Major Test. One Trusted Partner.", lead
 *     paragraph, 8 portrait cards) was deleted. With it goes the accent-colour inversion this
 *     file used to document: that green-eyebrow/orange-heading flip existed only for that
 *     section, so `.team__eyebrow`/`.team__accent` are gone and every eyebrow/accent left on the
 *     page (the CTA's) follows NGO's standard mapping via the shared utilities.
 *
 * REUSE: the hero is `SubPageHero`, the same component Consultancy's seven sub-pages use — the
 * redesign gave NGO the identical 1440×670 / 25%-scrim / bottom-120 / `u-page-title` treatment,
 * so it takes a `photo` prop rather than a second copy of the markup. The closing CTA is
 * `NgoCtaSection` — this page's copy of that markup and CSS moved there wholesale; see that
 * component for the node data and for why the rows are `Button`s.
 *
 * ⚠ A note here used to claim Home's CTA was a DIFFERENT (older) shape whose links were not
 * button instances, and left it alone on that basis. That was wrong: Home's rows are the same
 * `GIEVA Button` instances (componentId 5995:7321), in the live frame and in its own committed
 * node.json alike. Both pages now render `NgoCtaSection`.
 *
 * TYPE: the section headings use `u-h2`, not `u-section-title`. The design's headings are
 * `GIEVA.org/Arial/Heading 2` — 48/56/700 tracking **−0.26px** — and `u-section-title` resolves
 * its tracking to `--letter-spacing-display` (−3.3px, the 110px display step), which rendered
 * these visibly tighter than the frame. `u-h2` is the same size/line/weight with the right
 * tracking. Fixed page-locally on purpose: `--type-section-title-tracking` looks wrong at the
 * token layer too, but it feeds all 18 routes and is not this page's to change.
 *
 * Heading order: h1 "Who We Are" → h2 "Our Story" → h2 "Vision" → h2 "Mision" → h2 "Core Values"
 * → h3 per value → h2 "Ready to Join the Movement?". No level is skipped.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SubPageHero from '@components/SubPageHero.astro';
import NgoCtaSection from '@components/NgoCtaSection.astro';
import StatCounter from '@components/StatCounter.astro';
import { ngoHeroPhoto } from '@lib/ngo-hero-images';

const stats = [
  { value: '10,000+', label: 'Lives Changed' },
  { value: '30+', label: 'Global Partners' },
  { value: '12+', label: 'Years Active' },
  { value: '98%', label: 'Success Rate' },
];

/* Verbatim from the live node's text runs (12327:12081 → 12327:12096). */
const coreValues = [
  {
    title: 'Integrity',
    body: 'We uphold the highest standards of honesty, transparency, and accountability in everything we do. Our commitment to ethical practices builds trust with the students, families, partners, and communities we serve.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Inclusivity',
    body: 'We foster an environment where everyone is welcomed, respected, and given equal access to opportunities regardless of their background, gender, ability, or circumstance.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Innovation',
    body: 'We embrace creativity, technology, and forward-thinking solutions to address educational and social challenges, ensuring our programs remain relevant in an ever-changing world.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Service',
    body: 'Service is at the heart of who we are. We are dedicated to creating positive social impact by supporting communities, promoting volunteerism, and responding to the evolving needs of society.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Empowerment',
    body: 'We believe every individual deserves the opportunity to learn, lead, and succeed. Through education, mentorship, and skills development, we equip young people with the confidence and tools to shape their own futures.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Who We Are — GIEVA NGO"
  description="How GIEVA began, our vision and mission, and the values that guide 12+ years of impact across Nigeria."
  brand="ngo"
>
  <!-- ── Photo hero (node 12330:13416) ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <SubPageHero title="Who We Are" photo={ngoHeroPhoto} />

  <!-- ── Our Story: two-column copy + stats band ─────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section intro">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="u-h2 intro__title">Our Story</h2>

      <div class="intro__grid">
        <p class="u-body-lg">
          <strong>Global Integrated Education Volunteers Association (GIEVA)</strong> was registered
          in 2006 as a nonprofit organization to improve access to quality education and global learning
          opportunities among young Nigerians. Over the years, GIEVA has grown to serve over 1,000
          young Nigerians annually, with a strong focus on inclusive education, digital empowerment,
          and youth development.
        </p>
        <p class="u-body-lg">
          The concept for the Global Integrated Education Volunteers Association emerged in
          2005, and the organization was born in January 2007. The Birth of the organization
          was a result of the critical need to empower the present and future generation of
          global youth for sustainable development.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul role="list" class="stats">
        {
          stats.map((stat) => (
            <li class="stats__item">
              <p class="u-h2 stats__value">
                <StatCounter value={stat.value} />
              </p>
              <p class="stats__label">{stat.label}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Vision / Mission / Core Values (node 12327:12048) ────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section pillars">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pillars__grid">
        <div>
          <h2 class="u-h2">Vision</h2>
          <p class="u-body-lg pillars__body">
            To inspire youths to lead, innovate, and create equitable opportunities for all.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="u-h2">Mision</h2>
          <p class="u-body-lg pillars__body">
            Our mission is to nurture bold young leaders through transformative education,
            mentorship, and digital innovation, enabling them to create solutions and expand
            opportunities for a more equitable world.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="values">
        <h2 class="u-h2">Core Values</h2>
        <ul role="list" class="values__grid">
          {
            coreValues.map((value) => (
              <li>
                <h3 class="u-lead values__title">{value.title}</h3>
                <p class="u-body-lg values__body">{value.body}</p>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── CTA (node 12327:12132) — shared with /ngo, see NgoCtaSection.astro ───── -->
  <section class="section cta">
    <div class="container">
      <NgoCtaSection />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Shared section rhythm ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
     The live frame stacks its three body blocks 240px apart (story ends y=688, pillars start
     y=928; pillars end y=1736, CTA starts y=1976) and closes with 120px before the footer —
     i.e. 120px top and bottom per section, which is what --space-6xl already gives. The hero
     needs no bottom padding of its own: the story block's own 120px top is the whole gap. */
  .section {
    padding-block: var(--section-padding-block);
  }

  /* ── Our Story ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     node 12327:12012, 1312×568, reconciled: 56 (title) + 80 + 120 (copy) + 80 + 232 (stats). */
  .intro__title {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4xl);
    color: var(--color-mine-shaft);
  }
  .intro__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-xl); /* 676 − 636 = 40 */
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4xl);
    color: var(--color-mine-shaft);
  }

  /* Stats band (node 12327:12021). Each figure sits in its own 252×168 rounded box, and the
     boxes are separated by 1px full-height rules — not by borders on the boxes themselves.
     Reconciled across: 4×252 + 6×40 (gaps) + 2×32 (container padding) = 1312.
     Down: 32 + 56 (value) + 24 (gap) + 24 (label) + 32 = 168.
     The design also sets backdrop-blur 5px here; it is inert over the white page, so it is
     not reproduced. */
  .stats {
    display: flex;
    align-items: stretch;
    /* 80, not 40: the design's rules are zero-width flex *children*, so each sits between two
       40px gaps. Rendering them as pseudo-elements removes those children, and the 80px gap is
       what reproduces the same spacing — it lands each box at exactly the designed 252px
       (1312 − 64 padding − 3×80 = 1008; 1008 / 4 = 252). */
    gap: var(--space-4xl);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .stats__item {
    /* min-width:0 overrides flex's `auto` minimum, which would otherwise let the widest figure
       ("10,000+", 174px + 128px padding) push its own box past the other three. */
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    padding: var(--space-lg) var(--space-3xl);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    text-align: center;
  }
  /* The rule is a sibling element in the design, so it renders between items rather than as a
     border on one: 1px, #292929, and exactly as tall as the 168px box it sits beside. */
  .stats__item + .stats__item {
    position: relative;
  }
  .stats__item + .stats__item::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-block: 0;
    inset-inline-start: calc(var(--space-4xl) / -2);
    width: 1px;
    background: var(--color-mine-shaft);
  }
  /* The 64px inline padding is a minimum, not a clamp: "10,000+" measures 174px against the
     box's 124px inner width, and the design lets it overflow the padding rather than wrap
     (every figure and label in the frame is a single unwrapped line). Without `nowrap` the
     widest figure breaks after the comma. */
  .stats__value {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-mine-shaft);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .stats__label {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-mine-shaft);
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-size: var(--type-body-lg-size);
    line-height: var(--type-body-lg-line);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
  }

  /* ── Vision / Mission / Core Values ─────────────────────────────────────────
     node 12327:12049: two 636 columns 40 apart, heading→body 40 (y 56→96).
     node 12327:12071: 40 between the Core Values heading and the first row, 40 between rows,
     24 between each value's title and body. Reconciled: 56 + 3×(40 + 128) = 560. */
  .pillars__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4xl);
  }
  .pillars__grid h2,
  .values h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-mine-shaft);
  }
  .pillars__body {
    margin: var(--space-xl) 0 0;
    color: var(--color-mine-shaft);
  }
  .values__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }
  .values__title {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-mine-shaft);
  }
  .values__body {
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 0;
    color: var(--color-mine-shaft);
  }

  /* The CTA card's CSS (node 12327:12132) now lives in NgoCtaSection.astro, shared with /ngo. */

  /* ── Responsive ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     No tablet/mobile NGO About frame exists in the design; these are our authored,
     content-preserving reflows (same approach as the NGO Partners page). */
  /* The stats band has to break to 2×2 well before the text columns do: a row of four boxes
     needs 4×(174px figure + padding) + 3×80 gaps, so below ~1024px the un-wrappable figures
     overflow the page rather than the box (they are `nowrap` by design — see above). The
     rules are dropped once wrapped: they mark divisions in a single row, and a 2×2 grid has
     no single row to divide. */
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .stats {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: var(--space-xl);
      padding-inline: 0;
    }
    .stats__item {
      flex: 1 1 40%;
      padding-inline: var(--space-md);
    }
    .stats__item + .stats__item::before {
      content: none;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .intro__grid,
    .pillars__grid,
    .values__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
